      "type": "text",
      "value": ". Water is pumped from one tank to another through a piping system with a total pressure 13 drop of 150 psi. A control valve is provided in the piping loop to modulate the flow rates. Assume the key variables:"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Fluid temperature = 70 °F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Design (maximum) flow rate = 160gpm"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Operating flow rate = 110 gpm"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Minimum flow rate = 25 gpm"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Pipe diameter = 3 inches"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Specific gravity = 1.0"
    },
    {
